message: "If you use the Linguistic Kernel in research, please cite it as below."
title: "Linguistic Kernel: deterministic structural measurement of text"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Parrish
    given-names: Russell
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0009-0008-9781-7995
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: 2026-10-21
license: MIT
url: https://www.parallaxmetrology.com/linguistic_kernel_pm.html
repository-code: https://github.com/parallaxmetrology/linguistic-kernel
keywords: [llm evaluation, structural telemetry, deterministic metrics, text structure]
abstract: >
  A deterministic, model-free instrument that reduces a text to eight structural
  coordinates (weight shift, void, packing, cohesion, segmentation strain,
  peripheral pull, flow instability, structural thickness) with a countable
  evidence bundle, rhetorical-state and collapse labels, and corpus tools for
  fingerprints, comparison and drift envelopes. Wraps kernel v19.
